error[E0277]: `SchemaVersion` is one of the platform's tables, and a transaction does not read it
  --> tests/compile_fail/schema_version_read_on_bare_tx.rs:11:31
   |
11 |     let _versions = tx.scan::<SchemaVersion>()?;
   |                        ----   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `SchemaVersion` is read through `Db::snapshot`, never through a transaction
   |                        |
   |                        required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `ScopeReadableBy<Tx<'_>, SchemaVersion>` is not implemented for `charpente::charpente_core::table::PlatformOwned`
   = note: the platform's tables — the job queue (`JobRow`), the event log (`EventRow`) and the migration record (`SchemaVersion`) — are the platform's own state, and the first two hold every tenant's rows, so neither a handler nor a job reads them; code that holds the `Db` reads them through a snapshot:
               db.snapshot()?.scan::<SchemaVersion>()?
   = note: a route that shows a job's progress or an event's history reads a table of the app's own, written in the same transaction as the enqueue or the emit, or subscribes to the events
help: the trait `ScopeReadableBy<V, R>` is conditionally implemented for `charpente::charpente_core::table::PlatformOwned`
  --> $WORKSPACE/crates/charpente-core/src/table.rs
   |
   | impl<V: ?Sized + sealed::Operator, R> ScopeReadableBy<V, R> for PlatformOwned {}
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^----------------^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |                  |
   |                  unsatisfied requirement introduced here: `Tx<'_>: table::sealed::Operator`
   = note: required for `SchemaVersion` to implement `ReadableBy<Tx<'_>>`
note: required by a bound in `charpente::View::scan`
  --> $WORKSPACE/crates/charpente-core/src/table.rs
   |
   |     fn scan<R: UnscopedRow + ReadableBy<Self>>(&self) -> io::Result<Vec<R>>;
   |                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `View::scan`

